# COMPONENT

## KnowledgeWorkbench

### STYLE

full-fledged-with-standalone

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.knowledgeworkbench

### DESCRIPTION

Forms Information Candidates for human work. Supports starter registration/search
and provider-neutral proposal registration with durable source-key lookup. Sequential
resend returns the current candidate without overwriting edits or original proposal
metadata. Uses a stable standalone identity and the CNCF native persistent datastore.
Human formation, review and approval belong to subsequent Phase 1 Steps.

### COMPONENTLET

#### public-candidate

#### candidate-admin

# COMPONENTLET

## public-candidate

- component :: KnowledgeWorkbench
- kind :: participant

### DESCRIPTION

Declares the participant intended for public Candidate registration and search.
The current factory constructs only the primary participant; this declaration
does not enable MCP publication.

# COMPONENTLET

## candidate-admin

- component :: KnowledgeWorkbench
- kind :: participant

### DESCRIPTION

Declares the participant intended for administrative Candidate work. The current
factory does not instantiate this participant or publish its services through MCP.

# SERVICE

## Candidate

### DESCRIPTION

Registers and searches Information Candidates and source proposals for the current user.
Operations require a stable user identity and the native persistent application
datastore supplied by the CNCF Subsystem.

### OPERATION

#### registerCandidate

##### DESCRIPTION

Creates a native InformationCandidate using a required name and optional
description. This command persists a new entity and returns its native id and name.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCandidate

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterCandidateResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-create

##### ENTITY
InformationCandidate

#### registerProposal

##### DESCRIPTION

Validates one proposal JSON object and searches its exact producerRef/proposalId key.
Creates a native candidate when absent; sequential resend returns the current
candidate with created=false without any incoming-field write. Retains the exact
first originalProposal and supplied evidence/material/source references.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterProposal

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
RegisterProposalResult

#### findCandidateByProposal

##### DESCRIPTION

Finds the current accessible candidate by exact, case-sensitive producerRef and
proposalId. Returns an optional candidate without writes. Ambiguous visible
correspondence fails explicitly instead of selecting a row.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
FindCandidateByProposal

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
FindCandidateByProposalResult

#### listCandidates

##### DESCRIPTION

Returns accessible InformationCandidates as items. Optional text matches a
case-insensitive substring of name or description; without text, all accessible
rows are eligible. Optional offset and limit apply through native query paging.
This query does not create candidates.

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### INPUT

###### TYPE
ListCandidates

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE
ListCandidatesResult

##### IMPLEMENTATION
entity-search

##### ENTITY
InformationCandidate

# ENTITY

## InformationCandidate

### Attribute

| name        | type     | multiplicity |
|-------------+----------+--------------|
| id          | entityid | 1            |
| name        | name     | 1            |
| description | InformationCandidateDescription | ?            |
| producerRef | ProposalProducerRef | ? |
| proposalId | SourceProposalId | ? |
| sourceKind | ProposalSourceKind | ? |
| originalProposal | ProposalJsonText | ? |
| content | CandidateContent | ? |
| context | CandidateContext | ? |
| preparationState | ProposalPreparationState | ? |
| evidenceRefs | ProposalReference | * |
| preparedMaterialRefs | ProposalReference | * |
| sourceRunRef | ProposalReference | ? |
| sourceContextRef | ProposalReference | ? |

